ITEMS = ((('what is a dislocation and how it happens', 'how do i recognise a dislocation', 'what are the signs of a dislocation', 'what does a dislocation look like', 'how can i tell if it is a dislocation with a dislocation', 'what symptoms occur in a dislocation', 'how to spot severe dislocations', 'what should i look for in a dislocation', 'how do i know if dislocations are serious', 'what early signs of a dislocation are'), 'A dislocation is when a joint is forced out of position, often after a fall or impact. Signs include severe pain, swelling, a misshapen joint and inability to move it. Call emergency services and do not try to push it back.'), (('what immediate action helps a dislocation', 'how do i treat a dislocation', 'what is the first aid for dislocations', 'how to respond to a dislocation', 'what to do immediately in a dislocation', 'how do you handle dislocations', 'which measures help a dislocation', 'how can i assist with a dislocation', 'what is the best response to a dislocation', 'how should i care for a dislocation'), 'For a dislocation, support the joint in the position you find it and keep the person still. Cover any wound and call emergency services. Do not attempt to realign the joint yourself.'), (('should i try to put a joint back with a dislocation', 'can i reduce a dislocation myself', 'why not push a dislocated joint back with a dislocation', 'what if the joint looks obvious with a dislocation', 'should i pull on a dislocated arm with a dislocation', 'what happens if i force it with a dislocation', 'how to support the limb instead with a dislocation', 'when to call for help with a dislocation', 'what to tell the operator with a dislocation', 'who can reduce a dislocation safely'), 'Never try to push a dislocated joint back into place, as you can damage nerves and blood vessels. Support it with padding and keep the person still. Call emergency services for a qualified assessment.'), (('how do i support a dislocated shoulder with a dislocation', 'what to do for a dislocated elbow with a dislocation', 'how to hold a dislocated hip with a dislocation', 'what if a finger joint is out with a dislocation', 'how to keep the arm still with a dislocation', 'should i use a sling with a dislocation', 'what if there is no padding with a dislocation', 'how to check the skin colour with a dislocation', 'when to call urgent help with a dislocation', 'who can assess the joint with a dislocation'), 'Support a dislocated joint with your hands or soft padding in the position found, and use a sling for an arm if it can be done without moving it. Check fingers or toes stay warm and pink. Call emergency services.'), (('what if a dislocation breaks the skin', 'how to cover an open dislocation', 'should i wash the wound with a dislocation', 'what if there is bleeding with a dislocation', 'how to apply a dressing with a dislocation', 'what if bone is visible with a dislocation', 'should i press on the wound with a dislocation', 'how to protect the area with a dislocation', 'when should urgent help be called for a dislocation', 'who can treat an open injury with a dislocation'), 'If a dislocation has broken the skin, cover the wound with a clean dressing and call emergency services. Do not wash away visible bone or push it back. Keep the person still and warm while waiting.'), (('can a dislocation happen in a child', 'what to do for a child with a dislocated joint with a dislocation', 'how to tell in a toddler with a dislocation', 'what if a child will not move an arm with a dislocation', 'should i call an ambulance with a dislocation', 'how to comfort a child with a dislocation', 'what if the joint looks bent with a dislocation', 'how to support small limbs with a dislocation', 'when to take a child to hospital with a dislocation', 'who can examine a child with a dislocation'), 'Children can dislocate joints, sometimes after a fall or a pull on the arm. Support the limb and call emergency services rather than trying to fix it. A doctor can assess the injury and arrange imaging.'), (('what if feeling is lost after a dislocation', 'how to check circulation with a dislocation', 'what if fingers are cold with a dislocation', 'should i move the joint to check it with a dislocation', 'what if there is numbness with a dislocation', 'how to watch the skin with a dislocation', 'when is urgent help needed for a dislocation', 'what to report to the operator with a dislocation', 'how to keep the person calm with a dislocation', 'who can assess nerve injury with a dislocation'), 'Cold, pale or numb fingers or toes after a dislocation need urgent assessment. Do not move the joint to test it. Call emergency services and tell the operator about the changes in feeling and colour.'), (('what can i give for dislocation pain', 'should i give water with a dislocation', 'can i give tablets with a dislocation', 'what if the person is fasting with a dislocation', 'how to keep them comfortable with a dislocation', 'what not to give with a dislocation', 'when to ask a pharmacist with a dislocation', 'how to report medicine use with a dislocation', 'what if they are in shock with a dislocation', 'who can advise on pain relief with a dislocation'), 'Do not give food or drink to someone with a dislocation who may need treatment in hospital. Call emergency services and keep them comfortable. Tell the crew about any medicines the person takes.'), (('how can i prevent dislocations', 'what protects joints during sport with a dislocation', 'should i warm up with a dislocation', 'how to fall safely with a dislocation', 'what if i have loose joints with a dislocation', 'how to build muscle support with a dislocation', 'when to seek advice about joints with a dislocation', 'what equipment helps with a dislocation', 'how to avoid repeat injuries with a dislocation', 'who can advise on joint health with a dislocation'), 'Protective equipment, warming up and building muscle around joints can reduce dislocation risk. Ask a physiotherapist about exercises if your joints feel unstable. Seek medical advice after a first dislocation.'), (('when should i call emergency services for a dislocation', 'is a dislocation always urgent', 'what if the joint returns by itself with a dislocation', 'should i call for mild pain with a dislocation', 'what to report about the injury with a dislocation', 'how urgent is swelling with a dislocation', 'what if numbness occurs with a dislocation', 'when to go to hospital with a dislocation', 'how to keep the area still with a dislocation', 'which paramedic takes over after a dislocation'), 'Call emergency services for a suspected dislocation, especially with deformity, numbness or broken skin. Even if the joint seems to settle, it needs assessment. Keep the person still until help arrives.'))
